"""Template for an optional GitHub PAT (private forks only).

Official builds ship WITHOUT a token since v0.8.1 — the release repo is
public and anonymous reads work. CI no longer injects this file (the baked
PAT expiring is what broke every installed client's update check in
2026-09).

If you run a private fork: copy this to ``_token.py`` (gitignored) with a
PAT that has ``Contents: Read`` on your fork. Mind the expiry — a baked
token that expires bricks update checks for every installed build, and the
client can only fall back anonymously if the repo is public.
"""
TOKEN = ""
